# Conventional Commits. Subject line:

#   <type>(<optional scope>): <imperative summary in the imperative mood>
#
# Types:
#   feat      a new capability the user can see
#   fix       a bug fix
#   refactor  behaviour unchanged, structure changed
#   perf      a change made for speed or memory
#   docs      documentation only
#   chore     tooling, deps, config, housekeeping
#   test      adding or correcting tests
#
# Scopes used in this repo:
#   project   package identity, tooling, config
#   deps      dependency changes
#   ui        components and layout
#   a11y      accessibility, including contrast and keyboard
#   brand     name, copy, metadata
#   api       the scrape endpoint and the data layer
#   home      the home page
#
# Rules:
#   - subject under 72 characters, no trailing period
#   - explain WHY in the body, not WHAT the diff already shows
#   - note anything that surprised you, cost you time, or that you verified
#   - add a Co-Authored-By trailer for agent-authored commits
#
# Examples:
#   fix(a11y): restore checkbox and label association
#   feat(home): add FAQ accordion
#   chore(deps): swap ESLint for Biome, which supports TypeScript 7

type(scope): summary